{"id":"p08-l07","minutes":35,"summary":"Every causal filter delays the signal, and inside a feedback loop delay is phase lag taken straight from the stability margin. You define phase delay and group delay, compute them for FIR and IIR filters, measure the delay of a tone burst through a filter, and work out the phase a sensor filter costs a control loop.","html":"<h2 id=\"two-kinds-of-delay\">Two kinds of delay</h2>\n<p>A filter multiplies the sinusoid at frequency <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span></span></span></span> by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.138em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.888em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">j</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">φ</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Two delays follow from the phase:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Phase delay</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span></span></span></span>: how far a pure sinusoid’s crests shift.</li>\n<li><strong>Group delay</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span></span></span></span>: how far the <em>envelope</em> of a narrowband burst, its information, shifts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For a <strong>linear-phase FIR</strong> (lesson 4) both equal <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span> samples at every frequency, so the waveform keeps its shape. IIR filters have frequency-dependent delay, usually peaking near the cutoff, so a step’s shape changes (overshoot, ringing) even though the magnitude looks benign.</p>\n<h2 id=\"delay-in-a-control-loop\">Delay in a control loop</h2>\n<p>A pure delay <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> contributes phase <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and no change of gain. At the loop’s crossover frequency <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, a filter in the feedback path removes roughly</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">360°</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>from the phase margin (Phase 13), where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span></span></span></span> is the filter’s delay near <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. A 10 ms filter on a 20 Hz loop costs about 72°: often the whole margin. Hence the rules: filter only as much as needed, put the cutoff well above the crossover (5–10×), and count the ADC, the computation and the PWM update as delays too.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"groupdelay\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Group delay against frequency for four filters at 1 kHz. Move the control bandwidth to see how much phase each filter takes from the loop there.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A 4th-order Butterworth anti-noise filter at 50 Hz, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> kHz, sits in a loop with a 20 Hz crossover.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Group delay at 20 Hz: 8.94 samples, which is 8.94 ms.</li>\n<li>Phase at 20 Hz: −60.9°. A 60° phase margin is gone.</li>\n<li>Move the filter to 200 Hz instead: the phase at 20 Hz falls to about −15°.</li>\n<li>A 31-tap linear-phase FIR has 15 ms of delay at every frequency, which is 108° at 20 Hz: worse still. FIR linear phase is great for logging, costly in loops.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">group_delay.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> scipy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> signal\n\nFS = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000.0</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">group_delay</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">b, a, f, df=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span></span>):\n    w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * np.array([f - df, f + df]) / FS\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=w)\n    dphi = np.angle(H[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] / H[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>])                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># unwrap-free difference</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> -dphi / (w[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - w[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>])                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># in samples</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">burst_delay</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">b, a, f0, width=<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Delay of the envelope peak of a Gaussian tone burst through the filter, in samples.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    n = np.arange(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2000</span>)\n    env = np.exp(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * ((n - <span class=\"hljs-number\">600</span>) / width) ** <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>)\n    x = env * np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * f0 * n / FS)\n    y = signal.lfilter(b, a, x)\n    env_out = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(signal.hilbert(y))\n    num = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(env_out * n) / np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(env_out)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> num - <span class=\"hljs-number\">600</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    b, a = signal.butter(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>, fs=FS)\n    gd = group_delay(b, a, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>)\n    gd_ref = signal.group_delay((b, a), w=[<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>], fs=FS)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>][<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(gd - gd_ref) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(gd - <span class=\"hljs-number\">8.936</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>\n    meas = burst_delay(b, a, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;Butterworth 4 @ 50 Hz: group delay at 20 Hz <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{gd:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> samples, burst envelope delayed <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{meas:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(meas - gd) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=[<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>], fs=FS)\n    lag = -np.degrees(np.angle(H[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(lag - <span class=\"hljs-number\">60.92</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>\n    _, H200 = signal.freqz(*signal.butter(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>, fs=FS), worN=[<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>], fs=FS)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> -np.degrees(np.angle(H200[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>])) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>\n    h = signal.firwin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">31</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>, fs=FS)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> f <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(group_delay(h, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>], f) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-6</span>          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># linear phase: constant</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;phase lag at 20 Hz: Butterworth <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{lag:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> deg, 31-tap FIR <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">360</span>*<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>*<span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span>/FS:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>f}</span> deg&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A loop crosses over at 50 Hz with 45° of phase margin. What’s the largest total delay it can tolerate before going unstable?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The margin is gone when <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">360°</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">45°</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.5</span></span></span></span> ms. That includes sampling, computation, filters and the actuator update.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does a step through a Butterworth filter overshoot even though its magnitude response has no peak?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The group delay isn’t constant: components near the cutoff are delayed more than low frequencies, so they arrive late and pile up after the edge. The waveform changes shape even though no frequency is amplified.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p08-l07\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"two-kinds-of-delay","title":"Two kinds of delay"},{"id":"delay-in-a-control-loop","title":"Delay in a control loop"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p08-l07-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Group delay in samples of a 31-tap linear-phase FIR?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(N − 1)/2.</p>\n","answer":15,"tol":0.001,"unit":"samples"},{"id":"p08-l07-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase lag in degrees from a 10 ms delay at 20 Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>360° f T_d.</p>\n","answer":72,"tol":0.001,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p08-l07-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Maximum delay in ms for a 45° margin at a 50 Hz crossover?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Solve 360° f T_d = 45°.</p>\n","answer":2.5,"tol":0.001,"unit":"ms"},{"id":"p08-l07-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Group delay measures the delay of…</p>\n","explain":"<p>−dφ/dω.</p>\n","options":["DC","the envelope of a narrowband signal","a sinusoid’s crests only","the noise floor"],"answer":1},{"id":"p08-l07-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>To protect phase margin, a sensor low-pass cutoff should be…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Its phase lag at crossover stays small.</p>\n","options":["at the crossover","below the crossover","well above the crossover (5–10×)","as low as possible"],"answer":2},{"id":"p08-l07-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Group delay in ms of the 4th-order 50 Hz Butterworth at 20 Hz (f_s = 1 kHz)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>From the code.</p>\n","answer":8.936,"tol":0.002,"unit":"ms"}],"code":[{"file":"group_delay.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\nfrom scipy import signal\n\nFS = 1000.0\n\ndef group_delay(b, a, f, df=1e-3):\n    w = 2 * np.pi * np.array([f - df, f + df]) / FS\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=w)\n    dphi = np.angle(H[1] / H[0])                    # unwrap-free difference\n    return -dphi / (w[1] - w[0])                    # in samples\n\ndef burst_delay(b, a, f0, width=60):\n    \"\"\"Delay of the envelope peak of a Gaussian tone burst through the filter, in samples.\"\"\"\n    n = np.arange(2000)\n    env = np.exp(-0.5 * ((n - 600) / width) ** 2)\n    x = env * np.sin(2 * np.pi * f0 * n / FS)\n    y = signal.lfilter(b, a, x)\n    env_out = np.abs(signal.hilbert(y))\n    num = np.sum(env_out * n) / np.sum(env_out)\n    return num - 600\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    b, a = signal.butter(4, 50, fs=FS)\n    gd = group_delay(b, a, 20)\n    gd_ref = signal.group_delay((b, a), w=[20], fs=FS)[1][0]\n    assert abs(gd - gd_ref) < 1e-3 and abs(gd - 8.936) < 0.01\n    meas = burst_delay(b, a, 20)\n    print(f\"Butterworth 4 @ 50 Hz: group delay at 20 Hz {gd:.2f} samples, burst envelope delayed {meas:.2f}\")\n    assert abs(meas - gd) < 0.5\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=[20], fs=FS)\n    lag = -np.degrees(np.angle(H[0]))\n    assert abs(lag - 60.92) < 0.01\n    _, H200 = signal.freqz(*signal.butter(4, 200, fs=FS), worN=[20], fs=FS)\n    assert -np.degrees(np.angle(H200[0])) < 16\n    h = signal.firwin(31, 50, fs=FS)\n    for f in (5, 20, 40):\n        assert abs(group_delay(h, [1.0], f) - 15) < 1e-6          # linear phase: constant\n    print(f\"phase lag at 20 Hz: Butterworth {lag:.1f} deg, 31-tap FIR {360*20*15/FS:.0f} deg\")"}]}